"Signals Reforged" means the Minecraft mod Signals Reforged in every version and form in which cptgummiball
publishes it: the jar files, the compiled code in them, textures, models, icons, sounds, texts, language files,
data files (including the example layout structures) and documentation.

1. Ownership
   Signals Reforged is the property of cptgummiball. This license gives you limited rights to use it. It does not
   transfer any ownership, copyright or other rights. All rights not expressly granted here are reserved.

2. What you may do
   a) Download Signals Reforged from its official pages: https://modrinth.com/mod/signals-reforged,
      https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/signals-reforged and the releases of
      https://github.com/CptGummiball/SignalsReforged.
   b) Use Signals Reforged to play Minecraft: in singleplayer, and on your own or any other server.
   c) Show Signals Reforged in videos, streams, screenshots, reviews and guides.
   d) Use, copy and share layouts you build with it, including the example layout structures, in your worlds.

3. Modpacks
   You may include Signals Reforged in modpacks, public or private, free or paid, and distribute it as part of such
   a modpack, but only in its original, unmodified state: the jar files exactly as cptgummiball published them, not
   repackaged and not altered in any way. Where the modpack platform can link to the official download instead of
   copying the file, linking is preferred.

4. What you may not do
   Unless cptgummiball has given you written permission, you may not:
   a) modify, adapt, translate, patch or otherwise change Signals Reforged or any part of it, or create works derived
      from it, including modified jar files, forks, ports and re-textures;
   b) decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate or otherwise reverse engineer Signals Reforged, or attempt to obtain its
      source code, except where and only to the extent that applicable law expressly allows this despite this
      restriction;
   c) upload, mirror or distribute Signals Reforged anywhere other than as part of a modpack under section 3, or
      offer it as your own work;
   d) use the textures, models, icons, sounds or texts of Signals Reforged in other projects;
   e) remove or change this license or any copyright notice.

5. API for other mods
   Signals Reforged contains a documented API for other mods: the Java package dev.cptgummiball.signalsreforged.api.
   You may use the official Signals Reforged jar files and the API documentation as compile-only dependencies to
   develop, compile and distribute your own mods that work together with Signals Reforged (for example rail or cart
   adapters). Your mod may reference these classes, but must not contain them or any other part of Signals Reforged;
   players install Signals Reforged separately. Sections 1 and 4 apply to the API in all other respects.

